## 3. Adjudication

### 3.1 Fiber tier: outcomes (a) and (b) are structurally unreachable

The one-place hypothesis attaches to no pinned template object. The
fiber C is irreducible (f primitive, SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:29-30) with
>= 2 places forced by the template itself (P_1 != P_2, engine C10:
their series split at the characteristic level 32 since
a_1 - a_2 = 2 sqrt3 != 0), >= 4 places on the banked count
(SHEET6-CLASSICAL.md:156), generically 2 + r_B + 42
(GROK-MONODROMY.md:149-174). So (AM-SG) simply does not constrain C,
and no violation of it can kill residue-A — outcome (a) is unreachable.
Equally, no "CONSISTENT with margins" report (b) is honest: the
inequality is not satisfied-with-slack, it is inapplicable, and its
reflected form is violated. The violation is REQUIRED structure: by
(AM-JAC) a Keller counterexample's f must not be one-place, and this
template complies at the strongest (semigroup-certified) level.

Deformation stability: the reflected-ladder margins are the exponent
gaps m_{i+1} - m_i, which are POSITIVE for every admissible genome
(edges have positive length; any Q-preserving deformation keeps
ascending characteristic levels, i.e. y bounded along every y-side
place — the root-chart convention itself, SHEET6-TEMPLATE.md:63-64).
