+The degree-minimal clause is necessary: Theorem 2.1 shows that polynomial
+automorphisms can store arbitrarily long removable approximate-root chains
+at fixed `td`. The nonautomorphic/type/residue clauses are necessary because
+the unrestricted assertion is already false.
+
+An equivalent direct target for G2 is a uniform bound on the number of
+case-(II) `l=0` characteristic factors between the pole entry and its
+merge. A bound on the size of each factor is insufficient; repeated `2`
+already diverges.
